target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheNarrativeReadsARealFile'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    an interactive `looper pr-report` must not block on a read nobody is going to feed, which is what the character-device test prevents. The guard lives in its own function for a reason worth keeping: folded into readNarrative it could not be asserted, because the only observable difference between taking the branch and not taking it is whether a read happens, and the obvious fixture — /dev/null — returns the empty string either way. A cycle-2 agent proved the earlier test vacuous by deleting the whole guard and watching it stay green. The condition is DISABLED rather than the line deleted, because dropping it orphans `st` and a mutation that does not compile scores broken and tests nothing.
--- old
	return st.Mode()&os.ModeCharDevice == 0
--- new
	return st.Mode()&os.ModeCharDevice == 0 || true
